//? Title: Nested sampling: evidence and weighted posteriors
//? Subtitle: Actual finite walks, conserved prior mass and a truncated-Gaussian reference
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Estimate a likelihood averaged over a bounded uniform prior, while retaining
weighted posterior records. We begin with a constant likelihood whose evidence
is exactly known, then retain the original two-dimensional Gaussian experiment.
Actual producer traces expose discarded shells, finite constrained walks and
final live contributions, including a correction to the old remaining-mass
accounting.
)

\toc

> From prior mass to evidence

For likelihood L and normalized prior π, Z=∫L(θ)π(θ)dθ. Under suitable
continuous likelihood contours, prior mass above level λ defines a decreasing
X(λ), giving Z=∫₀¹L(X)dX. Ideal nested sampling repeatedly replaces the worst of
N live points with an independent constrained-prior draw. The expected log
shrinkage is−1/N; this implementation uses the deterministic schedule
X_i=exp(−i/N), rather than sampling shrinkages.

Its finite Gaussian walk begins at a randomly selected surviving live point,
proposes within the box and accepts only log likelihood strictly above the
discarded threshold. A finite walk need not mix, and it may retain a tied
starting survivor without any accepted move. These actual outcomes are recorded.
Neither independent constrained draws nor reliable exploration of separated
modes is guaranteed by this implementation.

> Constant likelihood: the complete mass partition

With L=1, any normalized prior has Z=1. Each discarded point owns
X_before−X_after, and all N final live points share the remaining X_final
equally. Their masses must sum to one even at zero iterations. The original code
incorrectly used the next discarded shell instead of X_final for final points.
This lost almost all the remaining mass when N was large and was especially
visible at zero iterations. The corrected producer uses log X_final−log N.
Constant-likelihood walks accept no strict proposals; that plateau does not
change the mass-accounting identity.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nested_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nested_sampling.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::nested_sampling_trace([](const auto &) {
        return 0.;
    }, {0.}, {1.}, 2, 2, 7, 2, {1000, 0});
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("prior", {0, 0}, "Uniform prior mass 1");
    std::print("| contribution | actual prior mass |\n| --- | ---: |\n");
    double sum = 0;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.iterations.size(); ++i) {
        double mass = std::exp(t.iterations[i].log_shell);
        sum += mass;
        auto id = std::to_string(i);
        d.node(id, {8, 2. - 3. * i},
               std::format("Dead {} shell {:.6f}", i, mass));
        d.edge("prior", id);
        std::print("| dead {} | {} |\n", i, mass);
    }
    double final = 0;
    for (auto &f : t.final_live)
        final += std::exp(f.log_prior_weight);
    sum += final;
    d.node("final", {8, -4}, std::format("Final live total {:.6f}", final));
    d.edge("prior", "final");
    std::print("| final live total | {} |\n\nTotal mass {}; log evidence {}.\n",
               final, sum, t.result.log_evidence);
    d.save_svg("build/nested_tiny.svg");
}
```
