> Retain the original Gaussian experiment

The original unnormalized likelihood is exp(−((x−2)²+(y+1)²)/2), with a uniform
prior on[-10,10]². The original controls are N=300, replacement cap8000, seed7
and40 walk proposals. The finite-box reference integrates both coordinates using
erf and divides by400. Replacing finite bounds by the whole plane yields
log(2π/400), numerically extremely close here, but the native reference retains
truncation.

The plot separates dead-point posterior weights from final-live weights,
displayed in thousandths to keep the small values readable. These are correlated
quadrature records with explicit normalized weights, not independent
equal-weight posterior draws. The program computes their weighted mean and
normalization directly. A single seeded result does not establish estimator
coverage or convergence.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nested_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nested_sampling.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r =
        dm::algorithms::nested_sampling(dm::algorithms::nested_sampling_demo_log_likelihood,
                                        {-10., -10.}, {10., 10.}, 300, 8000, 7,
                                        40);
    std::vector<double> dx, dw, lx, lw;
    double mass = 0, mx = 0, my = 0;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < r.posterior_samples.size(); ++i) {
        double w = std::exp(r.posterior_log_weights[i]);
        mass += w;
        mx += w * r.posterior_samples[i][0];
        my += w * r.posterior_samples[i][1];
        if (i < r.iterations) {
            dx.push_back(i);
            dw.push_back(1000 * w);
        } else {
            lx.push_back(i);
            lw.push_back(1000 * w);
        }
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(dx, dw, "dead records", {36, 105, 172}).points(lx, lw, "final live",
                                                           {192, 59, 50}, 2).title("Original Gaussian: actual normalized posterior weights").x_label("retained record index").y_label("posterior weight in thousandths").save_svg("build/nested_original.svg");
    std::print("| iterations | retained records | log evidence | finite-box reference | heuristic sqrt(H/N) " "| information | weight sum | weighted mean x | weighted mean y |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               r.iterations, r.posterior_samples.size(), r.log_evidence,
               dm::algorithms::nested_sampling_demo_log_evidence(),
               r.log_evidence_error, r.information, mass, mx, my);
}
```
