> Inspect actual walk decisions and the stopping heuristic

A smaller run makes the walk visible. Outside-box proposals skip the likelihood
callback. Inside proposals evaluate it and are accepted only above the actual
discarded threshold. Every proposal, acceptance count, surviving seed index,
old/new step scale and replacement is captured by the same producer. Scales
multiply by1.1 above50% acceptance and by0.9 otherwise, retaining the original
adaptation schedule.

After replacement, the stopping statistic is max observed live log
likelihood+log X_final−log Z_dead. It compares with log(10⁻⁴) by default. The
maximum observed live likelihood is not a proven maximum over undiscovered
regions, so this is a remaining-evidence heuristic rather than a rigorous bound.
Unlike the original code, it uses remaining mass rather than shell mass. Zero
remaining_fraction disables it for a fixed-budget diagnostic.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nested_walk.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nested_sampling.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::nested_sampling_trace(dm::algorithms::nested_sampling_demo_log_likelihood,
                                              {-10., -10.}, {10., 10.}, 10, 30,
                                              7, 8, {100000, 0});
    std::vector<double> ax, ay, rx, ry;
    std::size_t outside = 0, tied = 0;
    for (auto &q : t.proposals) {
        if (!q.in_box) {
            ++outside;
            continue;
        }
        if (q.accepted) {
            ax.push_back(q.point[0]);
            ay.push_back(q.point[1]);
        } else {
            rx.push_back(q.point[0]);
            ry.push_back(q.point[1]);
        }
    }
    for (auto &r : t.iterations)
        tied += !r.strict_replacement;
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(rx, ry, "rejected inside", {192, 59, 50}, 3).points(ax, ay,
                                                                 "accepted",
                                                                 {36, 105, 172},
                                                                 4).title(
        "Actual finite-walk proposals: fixed replacement budget").x_label(
        "x").y_label("y").save_svg("build/nested_walk.svg");
    std::print("{} actual proposals; {} outside; {} callbacks; {} replacements not strictly above " "threshold.\n",
               t.proposals.size(), outside, t.likelihood_calls, tied);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
240 actual proposals; 10 outside; 240 callbacks; 0 replacements not strictly above threshold.
\image(figures/nested_walk.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual accepted and rejected inside-box proposals from a fixed-budget run.)
\alttext(Outside proposals are counted separately and do not evaluate the likelihood; this plot does not claim independent samples.)

> Zero iterations, zero likelihood and guards

At zero iterations the estimate is the ordinary prior Monte Carlo mean of the N
likelihood values. Constant likelihood must therefore be integrated exactly up
to rounding for every tested budget. A callback may return negative infinity to
denote zero likelihood; if every retained contribution is zero, log evidence and
every log posterior weight are negative infinity. There is then no normalized
posterior. NaN and positive infinity are rejected.

All bounds are checked for nonempty equal shape, finite endpoints and finite
positive widths; at least two live points and one walk proposal are required.
Complete geometry is checked before callbacks. Trace admission counts2d+6
initial bound/control units,1+d per initial/proposal/final record,1+4d per
iteration and2+d per returned posterior record. Its default quota is1000000,
zero disables; online failure returns no partial result, but earlier callback
side effects remain. Ordinary production has no trace quota.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nested_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nested_sampling.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<std::string> labels;
    std::vector<double> z;
    std::print("| replacement budget | actual log evidence for constant L=1 | actual retained points |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t budget : {0, 1, 5, 20}) {
        auto t = dm::algorithms::nested_sampling_trace([](const auto &) {
            return 0.;
        }, {0.}, {1.}, 10, budget, 7, 2, {10000, 0});
        labels.push_back(std::to_string(budget));
        z.push_back(std::exp(t.result.log_evidence));
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", budget, t.result.log_evidence,
                   t.result.posterior_samples.size());
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(z, labels, "computed evidence");
    p.title("Constant likelihood: complete mass survives every budget").x_label(
        "replacement cap").y_label("estimated Z, exact reference 1").y_limits(
        0, 1.2).save_svg("build/nested_controls.svg");
    auto zero = dm::algorithms::nested_sampling_trace([](const auto &) {
        return -std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();
    }, {0.}, {1.}, 2, 0);
    std::print("\nAll-zero likelihood: zero-evidence status {}, log Z {}.\n",
               zero.zero_evidence, zero.result.log_evidence);
}
```
